EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:54322/postgres"

# ─── Google sign-in ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# No extra variables are needed here on purpose.
#
# The Google OAuth client ID and client SECRET are stored in the Supabase
# dashboard (Authentication → Providers → Google), and Supabase performs the
# token exchange with Google server-side. Putting them in an EXPO_PUBLIC_* var
# would ship them inside the JavaScript bundle, where anyone can read them.
#
# Setup, one time, in Google Cloud Console:
#   1. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create OAuth client ID → "Web application"
#   2. Authorised redirect URI:
#        https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#   3. Paste the client ID + secret into Supabase → Auth → Providers → Google
#
# A "Web application" client is the correct type even though this is a mobile
# app: the browser talks to Supabase, and Supabase talks to Google. Android/iOS
# OAuth client IDs are only needed for the native Google Sign-In SDK, which this
# app does not use (it would require a custom dev build and break Expo Go).
#
# Then allow-list the redirect targets in
# Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs:
#   upshot://**            (standalone / TestFlight / Play builds)
#   exp://**               (Expo Go during development)
